Module 1: User Management
FR-1.1 User Registration

Description

Users can create an account.

Acceptance Criteria

User enters:
Full name
Email
Password
Email must be unique.
Password is securely stored (later using hashing).
Success message displayed.
FR-1.2 Login

Users can log in using:

Email
Password

After successful login:

Redirect to Dashboard
Authentication token generated (Phase 5)
FR-1.3 Logout

Users can securely log out.

Module 2: Dashboard

Dashboard should display:

Welcome message
Upload Report button
Recent reports
Health summary
Quick statistics

Example:

Welcome Tamanna

Upload Report

Recent Reports

Total Reports : 8

Latest Upload : Aug 2026

Preferred Language : English
Module 3: Upload Report

Users can upload:

PDF
PNG
JPG
JPEG

Validation:

Maximum size (e.g., 10 MB)
Supported format only

After upload:

Report uploaded successfully.
Module 4: OCR

System extracts text from uploaded reports.

Input

Blood_Report.pdf

Output

Hemoglobin : 11.2

WBC : 7400

Platelets : 2.3 lakh
Module 5: AI Explanation

System converts medical text into simple language.

Example:

Input

Hemoglobin
11.2

Output

Hemoglobin carries oxygen in your blood.

Your value is slightly below the normal range.

This may have many possible causes, but only a healthcare professional can determine the reason.

Discuss these results with your doctor.
Module 6: Highlight Abnormal Values

The system compares extracted values against reference ranges (when available).

Display:

Test	Status
Hemoglobin	🔴 Low
WBC	🟢 Normal
Vitamin D	🔴 Low
Module 7: Medical Dictionary

Clicking a medical term should show:

What is it?

Why is it tested?

Normal range

General meaning of higher/lower values
Module 8: Translation

User chooses language.

Examples:

English
Hindi
Punjabi
Spanish

Entire explanation changes.

Module 9: Doctor Questions

Generate educational questions.

Example:

Should this test be repeated?
What symptoms should I monitor?
Could medications affect these results?
Are additional tests recommended?
Module 10: Report History

User can:

View previous reports
Search reports
Open report details
Delete report
Module 11: Analytics

Display trends over time.

Examples:

Hemoglobin graph
Blood sugar trend
Cholesterol trend
Module 12: Profile

User can update:

Name
Preferred language
Password
Profile photo (future)
